STEP 3 — CALL ANALYSIS
===================================================================

Classify the outcome of the call into exactly one of: "Business", "Sales", "N/A".

This is an OUTCOME classification, not an effort classification. The RM merely pitching, upselling, or sending a transaction link is NOT enough on its own for "Sales" or "Business" — the investor must have actually agreed to, committed to, or completed something during the call. If the RM pitched/pushed but the investor did not agree to anything (stayed non-committal, said "I'll think about it," went silent on it, or declined), that is "N/A", regardless of how much the RM tried.

- "Business": The investor's agreement went all the way to a completed/confirmed transaction on the call — e.g., the investor confirms the transaction/payment is done, RM confirms the investment/SIP has gone through, or the investor states they already invested during the course of the call.
- "Sales": The investor clearly AGREED to invest, upsell, or transact (verbally committed, accepted the transaction link with intent to act, agreed to an amount/fund) but the transaction is not confirmed as completed within the call itself.
- "N/A": The investor did not agree to invest, upsell, or transact — regardless of whether the RM pitched, upsold, sent a link, or created urgency. Also covers calls with no pitch attempt at all (servicing, portfolio/market update only, follow-up call).

